1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,270
Listen to a talk in a business class.

2
00:00:03,270 --> 00:00:08,440
Today, we're examining the concept of disruptive innovation

3
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,130
a term coined by Clayton Christensen.

4
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:14,229
Disruptive innovation refers to a process by

5
00:00:14,229 --> 00:00:19,100
which a smaller company with fewer resources successfully challenges established businesses.

6
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:23,650
This typically happens by targeting overlooked segments of the market,

7
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:30,020
offering simpler, cheaper or more convenient products that eventually appeal to a broader audience.

8
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:34,130
One classic example is the rise of digital photography.

9
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:38,190
Traditional film-based companies dominated the market for decades.

10
00:00:38,190 --> 00:00:41,611
However, digital cameras initially targeted amateur photographers

11
00:00:41,611 --> 00:00:46,010
and offered a new convenient way to take pictures.

12
00:00:46,010 --> 00:00:48,560
Over time, as technology improved

13
00:00:49,160 --> 00:00:51,104
digital photography appealed to professional photographers

14
00:00:51,104 --> 00:00:55,220
and everyday consumers drastically changing the industry

15
00:00:55,220 --> 00:00:58,050
and leading to the decline of film companies.

16
00:00:58,050 --> 00:01:00,311
Another example is streaming movie services,

17
00:01:00,311 --> 00:01:05,210
some of which started as DVD rental services that mailed movies to customers.

18
00:01:05,210 --> 00:01:10,070
They disrupted the video rental industry by focusing on consumer convenience.

19
00:01:10,070 --> 00:01:13,473
Then as broadband internet became more widespread,

20
00:01:13,473 --> 00:01:16,040
they adapted by introducing streaming services

21
00:01:16,380 --> 00:01:21,250
further disrupting established brick, and-mortar businesses that rented DVDs and videotapes.

22
00:01:21,250 --> 00:01:26,169
Disruptive innovation often requires companies to rethink their business models

23
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:29,120
and adapt to changing market conditions.

24
00:01:29,120 --> 00:01:35,010
Established businesses might fail to recognize the threat from new entrants until it's too late.

25
00:01:35,010 --> 00:01:39,894
Understanding disruptive innovation is crucial for businesses that want to avoid complacency

26
00:01:39,894 --> 00:01:43,150
and stay competitive in a rapidly evolving marketplace.
